WEBVTT

00:00.160 --> 00:05.160
Now analyzing the requirement, it is very important to understand which type of data warehouse you're

00:05.160 --> 00:09.280
going to go and build, because there is like not only one standard on how to build it.

00:09.280 --> 00:14.520
And if you go blindly implementing the data warehouse, you might be doing a lot of stuff that is totally

00:14.520 --> 00:17.760
unnecessary and you will be burning a lot of time.

00:17.760 --> 00:23.160
So that's why you have to sit with the stakeholders, with the department and understand what we exactly

00:23.160 --> 00:25.520
have to build and depend on the requirements.

00:25.520 --> 00:28.120
You design the shape of the data warehouse.

00:28.160 --> 00:30.480
So now let's go and analyze the requirement of this project.

00:30.520 --> 00:33.680
Now the whole project is split into two main sections.

00:33.680 --> 00:36.960
The first section we have to go and build a data warehouse.

00:36.960 --> 00:39.240
So this is a data engineering task.

00:39.240 --> 00:42.680
And we will go and develop Etls and data warehouse.

00:42.680 --> 00:48.520
And once we have done that we have to go and build an analytics and reporting business intelligence.

00:48.520 --> 00:50.520
So we're going to do data analysis.

00:50.520 --> 00:54.600
But now first we will be focusing on the first part building the data warehouse.

00:54.600 --> 00:55.760
So what do we have here.

00:55.760 --> 00:57.200
The statement is very simple.

00:57.360 --> 01:04.880
It says develop a modern data warehouse using SQL server to consolidate sales data enabling Ebling analytical

01:04.880 --> 01:07.640
reporting and informed decision making.

01:07.720 --> 01:09.600
So this is the main statement.

01:09.600 --> 01:11.240
And then we have specifications.

01:11.240 --> 01:12.920
The first one is about the data sources.

01:12.920 --> 01:17.520
It says import data from two source systems ERP and CRM.

01:17.520 --> 01:20.080
And they are provided as CSV files.

01:20.120 --> 01:22.920
And now the second task is talking about the data quality.

01:22.960 --> 01:27.960
We have to clean and fix data quality issues before we do the data analysis.

01:27.960 --> 01:31.520
Because let's be real, there is no raw data that is perfect.

01:31.560 --> 01:34.080
It is always missing you and we have to clean that up.

01:34.080 --> 01:36.880
Now the next task is talking about the integration.

01:36.880 --> 01:43.360
So it says we have to go and combine both of the sources into one single user friendly data model that

01:43.360 --> 01:46.120
is designed for analytics and reporting.

01:46.120 --> 01:50.640
So that means we have to go and merge those two sources into one single data model.

01:50.680 --> 01:52.440
And now we have here another specifications.

01:52.440 --> 01:55.160
It says focus on the latest data sets.

01:55.200 --> 01:57.440
So there is no need for historization.

01:57.440 --> 02:00.640
So that means we don't have to go and build histories in the database.

02:00.640 --> 02:03.280
And the final requirement is talking about the documentation.

02:03.280 --> 02:06.480
So it says provide clear documentations of the data model.

02:06.480 --> 02:12.240
So that means the last product of the data warehouse to support the business users and the analytical

02:12.240 --> 02:12.760
teams.

02:12.760 --> 02:16.680
So that means we have to generate a manual that can help the users.

02:16.720 --> 02:19.760
That makes lives easier for the consumers of our data.

02:19.760 --> 02:24.640
So as you can see, maybe this is very generic requirements, but it has a lot of informations already

02:24.640 --> 02:25.120
for you.

02:25.120 --> 02:28.320
So it's saying that we have to use the platform SQL server.

02:28.320 --> 02:33.800
We have two source systems using the CSV files, and it sounds that we really have a bad data quality

02:33.800 --> 02:34.640
in the sources.

02:34.640 --> 02:41.800
And as well it wants us to focus on building completely new data model that is designed for reporting.

02:41.800 --> 02:47.400
And it says we don't have to do historization and it is expected from us to generate documentations

02:47.400 --> 02:48.280
of the system.

02:48.280 --> 02:53.200
So these are the requirements for the data engineering part, where we're going to go and build a data

02:53.200 --> 02:55.960
warehouse that fulfill these requirements.

02:56.000 --> 02:56.320
All right.

02:56.320 --> 02:58.440
So with that we have analyzed the requirements.

02:58.440 --> 03:01.680
And as well we have closed the first easiest epic.

03:01.680 --> 03:02.920
So we are done with this.

03:02.920 --> 03:04.040
Let's go and close it.

03:04.040 --> 03:05.800
And now let's open another one.

03:05.800 --> 03:08.240
Here we have to design the data architecture.

03:08.240 --> 03:11.960
And the first task is to choose a data management approach.

03:11.960 --> 03:12.600
So let's go.
